jobs.description:
Our client is a rapidly growing international company operating in a highly innovative and industrial environment. Following significant growth and ambitious development projects, the Finance team continues to expand and is looking for a Senior Accountant to strengthen its operations.

Jobomschrijving

Reporting directly to the Head of Finance, you will join a growing finance team and play a key role in ensuring the reliability of the accounting function for the group's main Belgian entities.Your responsibilities will include:

• Managing the full accounting cycle from A to Z for the group's key Belgian entities;
• Participating in monthly, quarterly, and annual closings in compliance with Belgian GAAP;
• Preparing reconciliations, accruals, provisions, and financial reporting schedules;
• Supporting audit processes and ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial information;
• Collaborating closely with Business Controllers and operational teams in a project-driven environment;
• Contributing to the implementation and optimisation of accounting processes, controls, and reporting tools;
• Supporting consolidation and group reporting activities when required;
• Acting as a key finance partner in a fast-growing organisation undergoing continuous transformation;

• Bachelor's or Master's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field;
• Several years of accounting experience, ideally gained within an international, industrial, project-based, or fast-growing environment;
• Strong knowledge of Belgian GAAP is essential;
• Experience managing accounting activities independently and operating in a dynamic environment;
• Comfortable working with evolving processes and taking ownership of responsibilities;
• Strong analytical skills and attention to detail;
• Proactive, hands-on, and solution-oriented mindset;
• Fluent in French and/or English;

Our client is an established international organisation with its headquarters in Nivelles. As part of an important organisational transformation, the company is redesigning its Target Operating Model to strengthen collaboration, clarify responsibilities and establish more efficient and consistent ways of working across the Group.

Jobomschrijving

As a Freelance Senior Project & Process Manager (TOM) your responsibilities are:

• Lead the planning, coordination and execution of TOM design and implementation activities across the Group ;
• Structure project workstreams, milestones, deliverables and implementation plans ;
• Monitor dependencies, risks and issues, ensuring progress and alignment with business priorities ;
• Coordinate stakeholders, facilitate project meetings and support decision-making ;
• Prepare management updates and ensure clear communication on project progress ;
• Translate agreed TOM deliverables into concrete actions and sustainable implementation ;
• Support change management and the adoption of new organisational practices ;

A successful Freelance Senior Project & Process Manager (TOM) should have:

• At least 8 years of experience in project management, business transformation, operational excellence, business process management or organisational design ;
• Proven track record in leading complex, cross-functional transformation projects ;
• Strong project management and stakeholder management capabilities ;
• Excellent knowledge of business process mapping, workflow analysis and structured documentation ;
• Ability to translate complex business activities into clear, practical processes and ways of working ;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the confidence to challenge existing practices constructively ;
• Fluent in French & English ;

Our client is a well-established Belgian group with a strong international footprint, operating in the services and insurance environment.

Jobomschrijving

Reporting to the Accounting Manager, you will take end-to-end ownership of the Group's consolidation activities, covering both Belgian GAAP and IFRS scopes.Your main responsibilities will include:

• Managing the end-to-end consolidation process across Belgian and international entities, covering both Belgian GAAP and IFRS reporting;
• Performing key consolidation operations, including intercompany eliminations, IFRS adjustments and foreign currency conversions;
• Preparing reliable consolidated financial reporting and coordinating the different closing cycles;
• Taking ownership of two consolidation scopes, including international entities and an IFRS scope mainly linked to insurance and real estate activities;
• Harmonizing accounting practices and ensuring consistency and quality of financial information across entities;
• Working closely with Accounting, Controlling, Tax, Treasury, M&A and external auditors;
• Improving consolidation tools, processes, reporting and internal controls;
• Building and further developing the consolidation function, with the ambition to move towards more frequent consolidation cycles.

• Master's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics or a related field;
• Around 5 to 7 years of relevant experience, with hands-on, end-to-end consolidation experience;
• Strong knowledge of Belgian GAAP and consolidation principles, with IFRS experience highly valued;
• Previous exposure to the insurance sector would be a strong asset;
• Comfortable working with Excel and consolidation/ERP tools;
• Good command of French, Dutch and English;
• Hands-on, autonomous and proactive, with the ability to thrive in an environment where processes are still evolving;
• Ambitious and eager to take ownership of a function and contribute to its future development.
